## 🖥️ Compute environment

This project targets **PyTorch**{% if compute_backend == 'cuda' %} on **NVIDIA GPUs**{% endif %}:

- **Python** {{ python_version }}+
- **PyTorch** `{{ torch_version }}` / **torchvision** `{{ torchvision_version }}`
- **Compute backend**: {% if compute_backend == 'cuda' %}CUDA **{{ cuda_version }}**, with wheels from the PyTorch
  index for that version
  (`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu{{ cuda_version | replace('.', '') }}`){% else %}CPU, with wheels from the PyTorch CPU
  index (`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu`){% endif %}, configured in
  [`pyproject.toml`]({{ repo_file }}pyproject.toml); `uv sync` installs them.

### Switching the compute backend

The backend is the `[[tool.uv.index]]` named `pytorch` in
`pyproject.toml` (`cu126` / `cu128` / `cu130`, or `.../whl/cpu`).
After changing it, re-resolve with `uv lock && uv sync`, or re-run
`copier update --UNSAFE --vcs-ref pytorch` and answer
`compute_backend` / `cuda_version` again.

